<title>GERMANY: T-Mobil, Debis plan venture.</title>
<headline>T-Mobil, Debis plan venture.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Telekom unit T-Mobil and Daimler-Benz AG unit Debis plan to start a traffic telematics services venture that will have sales of 200 million marks within three years, Telekom said on Friday.  </p>
<p>The two partners, who will hold equal shares in the venture, see the market potential for telematics at about three million customers in Germany within a few years, Telekom said.</p>
<p>The service, which will be aimed at business and private customers, will include satellite-linked auto navigation systems, emergency calling and individual traffic reports. Service is likely to begin this summer.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
